WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.220
Sumo wrestlers eat up
to 7,000 calories a day

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.210
and weigh 300 to 400 pounds

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.903
or two to three times as
much as the average adult.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.770
While that may not sound like
the healthiest lifestyle,

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:18.800
you shouldn't judge a book,
or a body, by its cover.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.650
Take a closer look, and you'll discover

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:24.540
that it really is what's
on the inside that counts.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.190
Normally, people with
obesity store a portion

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:30.320
of their extra fat deep
inside the abdomen,

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.080
where it wraps around the pancreas,

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.580
liver, and other vital organs.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.413
We call this visceral fat.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.943
It pollutes the blood with molecules

00:00:38.943 --> 00:00:42.470
that can cause inflammation,
and this is why obesity

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:45.260
can lead to health issues
like high blood pressure,

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:48.660
Type 2 diabetes, and heart attacks,

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:52.210
but sumo wrestlers don't usually
suffer from these symptoms.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.124
So what's their trick?

00:00:54.124 --> 00:00:56.230
CT scans reveal that sumo wrestlers

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:58.580
don't have much visceral fat at all.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.330
Instead, they store most of their fat

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.520
right underneath the skin.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.840
That's why scientists think
sumo wrestlers are healthy.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.950
They have normal levels of triglycerides,

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.670
a type of fat in their blood,

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.530
and unexpectedly low
levels of cholesterol,

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:13.467
both of which lower their risk

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:16.550
of heart disease, heart
attack, and stroke.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.883
So how did they hit the jackpot on fat?

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.950
The secret's in their name: sumo wrestler.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.702
Studies show that intense exercise

00:01:26.702 --> 00:01:29.720
may prevent the buildup of visceral fat.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:31.720
Basically, it has to do with how exercise

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.830
increases a hormone called adiponectin.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.500
Adiponectin guides
glucose and fat molecules

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.180
out of our blood stream,
where they could build up

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:43.823
as visceral fat, and instead
puts them underneath the skin.

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:48.463
Mind you, sumo wrestlers
get a lot of exercise.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:52.480
At a sumo stable, or heya, in Japan,

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:54.900
training starts as early as 5 a.m.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.140
and can last for up to
five hours straight,

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.230
and it's nothing like
what you'd expect to find

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.780
at your typical group fitness class.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:06.660
For example, during an exercise
called butsukari-geiko,

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.110
wrestlers take turns
repeatedly hitting and pushing

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:11.440
each other until they
collapse to the floor

00:02:11.456 --> 00:02:13.558
from exhaustion.

00:02:13.558 --> 00:02:16.250
And then, of course, there's the match,

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:19.270
where wrestlers try to shove
their opponent out of the ring

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:22.130
or force them to touch the
ground with any body part

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:24.550
other than the soles of their feet.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:29.170
But as soon as the exercise
stops, so does its benefits.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.130
When sumo wrestlers retire, they have

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:33.530
to seriously cut calories or they become

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:36.120
at risk for cardiovascular disease.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.170
That might explain why retired wrestlers

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.970
reportedly die an
estimated 10 years younger

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.933
than the average Japanese citizen.

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.660
So while the thought of
eating 7,000 calories a day

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:50.230
might be appealing,
you probably shouldn't.

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.090
Unless you're spending most of your day

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:54.779
trying to topple a 400-pound man.

